2026-09-13T02:11:32.7591995Z [36;1m[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7592252Z [36;1m# Compile on every core the runner has, not the two this used to pin.[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7592615Z [36;1m# Standard GitHub-hosted Linux runners have been 4-vCPU since 2024, so[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7592950Z [36;1m# -j2 left half the box idle through the phase that dominates a build:[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7593261Z [36;1m# measured on a 4-core box, 8 vendored unity objects with ccache[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7593572Z [36;1m# disabled take 70.8 s at -j2 and 43.1 s at -j4 -- 1.64x, at identical[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7593898Z [36;1m# user time. Peak RSS per unity object is ~834 MB, so four in flight is[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7594169Z [36;1m# ~3.3 GB of the runner's 16 GB.[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7594433Z [36;1m# detectCores() can return NA on exotic platforms; fall back to the old[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7594770Z [36;1m# value there. `--as-cran` sets _R_CHECK_LIMIT_CORES_, but that polices[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7595225Z [36;1m# the *package's* runtime parallelism, not compilation, so this is safe.[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7595644Z [36;1mncores="$(Rscript --vanilla -e 'n <- parallel::detectCores(); cat(if (is.na(n) || n < 1) 2L else as.integer(n))')"[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7596029Z [36;1mecho "MAKEFLAGS = -j${ncores}" >> ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7596277Z [36;1mecho "===== generated ~/.R/Makevars ====="[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7596487Z [36;1mcat ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7596680Z [36;1mecho "==================================="[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7596883Z [36;1m[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7597093Z [36;1mecho 'CCACHE_SLOPPINESS=locale,time_macros' | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7597346Z [36;1m[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7597560Z [36;1m# Do NOT export UserNM here, however tempting the `UserNM=true` trick[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7597898Z [36;1m# from AGENTS.md looks. It is a development shortcut, not a CI setting.[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7598147Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7598316Z [36;1m# R takes the nm program from $UserNM in[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7598589Z [36;1m# tools:::read_symbols_from_object_file, and that function serves two[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7598910Z [36;1m# callers, not one: building `symbols.rds` at install time (which[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7599195Z [36;1m# src/Makevars puts on the `all:` target), *and*[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7599484Z [36;1m# tools:::check_so_symbols scanning the built .so during `R CMD check`.[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7599809Z [36;1m# Pointing nm at `true` blinds the second one, so the check finds no[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7600236Z [36;1m# symbols at all and reports "Found no calls to 'R_registerRoutines',[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7600574Z [36;1m# 'R_useDynamicSymbols'" -- a NOTE, and with error_on = "note" a failed[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7600898Z [36;1m# check on a package that registers its routines perfectly well.[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7601153Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7601375Z [36;1m# It is not worth scoping to the installs either: measured, the sweep is[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7601697Z [36;1m# ~0.25 s per 90 MB of unstripped objects, so ~10-20 s for the whole[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7602005Z [36;1m# ~2.5 GB tree -- under 5% of a commit's floor, against a footgun that[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7602279Z [36;1m# silently weakens a CRAN check.[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7602467Z [36;1m[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7602644Z [36;1m# echo 'CCACHE_DEBUG=true' | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7603118Z [36;1m# echo "CCACHE_DEBUGDIR=$(dirname $(pwd))/ccache-debug" | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7603544Z [36;1m# mkdir -p $(dirname $(pwd))/.ccache-debug[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:32.7603751Z [36;1m[0m
