2026-09-13T02:11:43.9696389Z [36;1m# The persistent ccache below is keyed on getRversion(), and that key is[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9696806Z [36;1m# only honest for a released R, where the version number changes[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9697159Z [36;1m# whenever the installation does. R-devel is rebuilt every day but keeps[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9697509Z [36;1m# reporting the same number for months, so one cache entry ends up[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9697845Z [36;1m# serving an arbitrary span of R-devel snapshots -- and restoring it in[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9698190Z [36;1m# the rcc R-devel job has produced build failures. Skip the persistent[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9698533Z [36;1m# cache there and build cold; ccache itself stays configured by the[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9698841Z [36;1m# install action, so reuse within the job is unaffected.[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9699080Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9699305Z [36;1m# R.version$status is empty for a released R and non-empty for one that[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9699643Z [36;1m# moves under a fixed version number ("Under development (unstable)" for[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9700001Z [36;1m# R-devel, "Patched" for R-patched) -- exactly the builds the key cannot[0m
2026-09-13T02:11:43.9700263Z [36;1m# tell apart.[0m
