2026-09-13T02:14:37.3632651Z Skipping the duckdb test suite.
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3632777Z 
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3632969Z The duckdb tests exercise DuckDB's bundled C++ engine and are deliberately
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3633335Z NOT run on CRAN. They run automatically on GitHub Actions (including
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3633697Z r-universe). This keeps check time and resource usage on CRAN within
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3634071Z acceptable limits and helps release duckdb in a predictable and controlled
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3634391Z manner.
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3634472Z 
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3634665Z This is intentional, not an oversight. duckdb has an extensive test suite
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3635225Z that runs continuously in our own CI; see <https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-r>.
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3635442Z 
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3635637Z To run the test suite locally, set the environment variable before checking:
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3635991Z   Sys.setenv(DUCKDB_R_RUN_TESTS = "true")    # from within R, or
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3636336Z   DUCKDB_R_RUN_TESTS=true R CMD check ...      # from the shell
2026-09-13T02:14:37.3636655Z ==============================================================================
